{"key":"ics/T0867","id":"T0867","name":"Lateral Tool Transfer","domain":"ics","platforms":["None"],"environments":["ics-ot"],"source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T0867","technique_page":"techniques/ics/T0867/","page":"detections/ics/T0867/","status":"guidance_only","counts":{"sigma":0,"atlas_basic":0,"atlas_anomaly":0,"strategies":1,"analytics":1,"live_validated":0},"sigma_rules":[],"atlas_basic":[],"atlas_anomaly":[],"anomaly_types":[],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0745","name":"Detection of Lateral Tool Transfer","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0745","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--62587e44-0623-4b14-bd45-126430eaed4a","relationship_id":"relationship--c563bfb5-173f-4a96-812b-2aad8057f09f","description":"","analytics":[{"id":"AN1878","name":"Analytic 1878","guidance":"Monitor for unexpected network share access, such as files transferred between shares within a network using protocols such as Server Message Block (SMB).\nMonitor for alike file hashes or characteristics (ex: filename) that are created on multiple hosts. \nMonitor for file creation in conjunction with other techniques (e.g., file transfers using Remote Services).\nMonitor for unusual processes with internal network connections creating files on-system which may be suspicious. \nMonitor executed commands and arguments for abnormal usage of utilities and command-line arguments that may be used in support of remote transfer of files.\nMonitor newly constructed processes that assist in lateral tool transfers, such as file transfer programs.\nMonitor for network traffic originating from unknown/unexpected hosts. Local network traffic metadata (such as source MAC addressing) as well as usage of network management protocols such as DHCP may be helpful in identifying hardware.","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0745#AN1878","platforms":["None"],"tuning":[],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0102","component":"Network Share Access","name":"Network Share